=====Usage notes=====
* Japanese does not generally distinguish between mice and rats, and both are commonly called ''nezumi''. If a distinction is needed, speakers may use the adjectives {{ja-r|大きい|おおきい|[[large]]}} or {{ja-r|小さい|ちいさい|[[small]]}}, or may use the word {{ja-r|マウス||[[mouse]]|pos=borrowed from either German or English}}.
* {{ja-uk}}
* {{U:ja:biology|ネズミ}}
* Although {{ja-r|子%年|ねずみ%どし|{{q|[[Chinese zodiac]]}} {{w|Year of the Rat}}|pos=also {{ja-r|子%年|ね%どし}}}} does derive from this same term ''nezumi'', it is not written with the [[kanji]] {{lang|ja|鼠}}.

