{{liushu|p}} – a bamboo Pan flute in which two mouths ([[吅]]) perhaps indicate the round top of the bamboo pipes. In the bronze inscriptions, {{zh-l|*亼}} (a flipped {{zh-l|*口}}) was added on top to show a mouth playing the instrument.

''{{w|Shuowen}}'' interprets it as an {{Han compound|品|侖|ls=ic|nocap=y}}, however his analysis does not match the original appearance. The bottom component is identical but unrelated to [[冊]] since it originally represents bamboo slips. The whole character is similar but unrelated to [[侖]].

